# ============================================================
# Salve — a Decursive replacement for Midnight (12.1.0)
# ============================================================
# No libraries, no Ace3, nothing embedded. The whole addon is the files below.
#
# THE ONE RULE THIS ADDON IS BUILT AROUND: aura data is SECRET in Midnight.
# Tainted Lua may store, pass and concatenate a secret, but may NOT compare it,
# do arithmetic on it, take its length, index it, or use it as a table key.
# Breaking that raises "execution tainted" every frame -- which is what killed
# Decursive and what makes the other replacements unusable.
#
# So Salve never reads an aura. It hands regions to Blizzard's AuraContainer
# under HARMFUL plus native dispel-type candidates and lets the engine drive
# them.
# See Features/AuraBinding.lua for the full argument.

# Namespace and saved variables. Everything else assumes these exist.
Core.lua
Core\Config.lua

# What to cast. Detection is Blizzard's job (the aura filter); this is only
# needed to give the secure button a spell name.
Features\Dispel.lua

# The engine binding. The heart of the addon.
Features\AuraBinding.lua

# When the panel is on screen. A state driver, not Show/Hide -- read the header.
Features\Visibility.lua

# Which mouse button casts what.
Features\Bindings.lua

# Movement-impairing effects and the class spells that remove them.
Features\Escape.lua

# Alert sounds and the loader for bundled, instance-scoped Salve_Data_* modules.
Features\Sound.lua

# ☠ Box.lua and Handle.lua before Panel.lua: Panel builds both from Create().
UI\Box.lua
UI\Handle.lua
UI\Panel.lua
# Optional LibDataBroker launcher. Registers nothing when LibStub is absent, and
# never owns the minimap button -- read the header before changing that.
UI\Broker.lua
UI\Minimap.lua

# Options. The first page becomes the root AddOns category; the rest are
# player-facing tasks rather than internal frame objects.
# ☠ Shared.lua first: every page below calls its widget helpers at file scope.
Options\Shared.lua
Options\Salve.lua
Options\Visibility.lua
Options\Dispel.lua
Options\Troubleshooting.lua
Options\Commands.lua
Options\About.lua

# Event routing and slash commands. Last, so everything they dispatch to exists.
Core\Events.lua
Core\Slash.lua
